  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_harold",
      "name": {
        "en": "Harold's Badge",
        "zh": "哈洛德证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_harold",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Harold has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for wide-range healing in tandem with remedying Operators of their accrued Elemental Injuries.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Medic Operator during field operations to exercise Wandering Medic responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员哈洛德擅长大范围治疗并为干员恢复元素损伤\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为医疗干员，行使行医职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_harold",
      "name": {
        "en": "Legs Care Kit",
        "zh": "腿部护理套装",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_harold",
      "description": {
        "en": "Lisburn,\nI received the Legs Care Kit you so kindly sent my way. It works splendidly! This old soldier, with but one leg to his name, no longer must weather the winter's bite in agony. But I must admit, I was taken aback to learn it hails from the pharmaceutical venture recently founded by Freya's brother. Why, that poor lad was still dwelling in squalor when I was on assignment in Kjerag! It seems he's amassed quite a fortune from peddling his medicines to the Victorians, hasn't he? A new company and all its trappings!\nHowever, upon scrutinizing the spray's formula, I couldn't help but notice its striking resemblance to the concoction I once used for mending fractures on burdenbeasts. Just a few additional herbs from Kjerag, and it performs like no other remedy I've encountered. Truly, you must be under Kjeragandr's divine protection.\nEverything good with you and Freya? How is the burdenbeast rental business going? You mentioned plans to build an abode by the Lake Silberneherze—why have I not yet seen any photographs of this endeavor? I eagerly await the day I can pay a visit to you both. And some good news: I spoke with the Chief of the Silverash Family about you and Freya, and I am pleased to report he did not oppose your union. Live your lives well, my friend.\nSpeaking of which, I find it quite difficult to fathom the intricacies of a Kjerag wedding. Forgive my curiosity, but do you exchange your vows by the serene waters of Lake Silberneherze or in Hoff Angrsaal? Before the revered statue of Kjeragandr? Must the parents of the betrothed be present as well? Regardless, I wish you a joyous marriage. And should any of your burdenbeasts suffer a broken leg once more, simply let me know.\nAfter all, when people's fortune in war is as grim as mine, we have no other choice but to help each other 'replant legs', and carry on. I may be a noble, but a fancy hat does not change the nature of this hapless creature underneath. I may possess the knowledge to mend the limbs of burdenbeasts, yet I remain at a loss when it comes to mending my own, or those of others. Allow this old cripple to extend his pity to his 'own kind'—Might you, through your pharmaceutical connections, explore whether there are other Victorian soldiers in need of their legs 'replanted'?\nI earnestly hope that, in the near future, everyone may walk on strong, healthy legs.\nHarold",
        "zh": "里斯本：\n你送的腿部护理套装我收到了，效果很不错，让我这个只剩一条好腿的糟老头在天气变冷的时候也不用那么痛苦了。没想到的是，这居然是芙蕾雅哥哥新开的药厂生产的。我记得我在谢拉格执行任务的时候，他还是当地出了名的穷小子呢！他这两年靠着向维多利亚人卖药竟然赚了这么大一笔，连厂都办起来了。\n不过，我研究了一下这喷雾的配方，这不是我当年给驮兽接腿用的药方吗？只是多加了几味原产自谢拉格的草药便有如此效果，耶拉冈德确实护佑着你们。\n你和芙蕾雅怎么样，驮兽租赁的生意顺利吗？你上上次说要在银心湖边建个小楼，怎么连照片都没给我寄过来，我还指望哪天去谢拉格住你们家呢。我此前和希瓦艾什家族的族长提过你和芙蕾雅的事，好消息是，他原则上并不反对你们的结合，好好过自己的日子，兄弟。\n说起来，我实在难以想象和谢拉格人结婚是一种什么样的体验，要经过什么步骤？请原谅我的好奇心，新人需要去银心湖、安格尔殿在耶拉冈德像前办什么仪式吗？双方父母需要到场吗？总而言之，祝你新婚快乐，希望我未来还有机会去给你们受伤的驮兽接腿。\n说到底，我们这些战争中的倒霉蛋，不靠彼此“接腿”，谁又能来帮我们呢。我虽然是贵族，也不过是戴着贵族帽子的老倒霉蛋罢了，我有一身接驮兽腿的手艺，但我接不了自己的坏腿，更没有精力接你们所有人的腿。请允许一个丢了腿的可怜老头儿对自己的“同类”怀有怜悯之心——不知道你是否有机会通过药厂渠道去调查一下，还有多少维多利亚的士兵需要“接腿”？\n愿大家在不远的未来，都能拥有健康的双腿。\n哈洛德",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
